    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0052_f7a3051ce53d.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 218px;\" /></p><p>Component of the force perpendicular to the ground,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mi>sin</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p><p>Now for equilibrium along vertical direction, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>F</mi><mi>sin</mi><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>800</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p>"
